+2. **Specialized Memory Architectures:** Use of on-chip buffers, FIFOs, or precalculated weight memories to manage bandwidth constraints and ensure conflict-free access to volume data [S1, unofficial].
+3. **Fixed-Point or Low-Precision Arithmetic:** Many custom units (e.g., VIRIM, Cube) utilize 16-bit precision for density and gradient values to maximize throughput and minimize hardware complexity [S1, unofficial].
+4. **Pipeline Parallelism:** Data flows through distinct stages (resampling $\rightarrow$ buffering $\rightarrow$ shading/compositing) often with asynchronous buffering to hide latency [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Hardware-based Geometry Unit Resampling](3139-hardware-based-geometry-unit-resampling.md)
-Implements a dedicated ASIC geometry unit for perspective calculations and resampling. It solves the high cost of geometry operations (consuming ~80% of software time) by using specialized logic for address generation and interpolation, achieving up to 640 MB/s bandwidth. Distinguished by precalculated interpolation weights and Sobel filter-based gradient estimation within the VIRIM architecture.
+Implements a dedicated ASIC geometry unit for perspective calculations and resampling. It solves the high cost of geometry operations by using specialized logic for address generation and interpolation. Distinguished by precalculated interpolation weights and Sobel filter-based gradient estimation within the VIRIM architecture. Choose when high-speed backward-mapping interpolation and gradient estimation are required.
 
 ### [Hardware-based Direct Volume Ray Casting](5442-hardware-based-direct-volume-ray-casting.md)
-Offloads ray-casting and shading to programmable DSPs. It solves the CPU bottleneck by decoupling fast geometry resampling from slower shading computations using a FIFO buffer. Focuses on image quality and flexible illumination (shadows) via object-order ray casting, utilizing a custom memory architecture.
+Offloads ray-casting and shading to programmable DSPs. It solves the CPU bottleneck by decoupling fast geometry resampling from slower shading computations using a FIFO buffer. Distinguished by its use of programmable DSPs rather than fixed-function logic, prioritizing image quality and algorithmic flexibility. Choose when complex illumination models and shadows are needed.
 
 ### [Custom Hardware Rendering](5746-custom-hardware-rendering.md)
-Refers to direct volume rendering via dedicated, non-standard graphics hardware like the Cube and VolumePro systems. It addresses the need for real-time rendering by using voxel processors that traverse data in memory order and sample processors for compositing. Unlike siblings, it relies on bespoke silicon pipelines rather than reconfigurable logic or DSP arrays.
